-- title:
--   Self-adjoint perfect pairing and rank formula on a Hecke corner
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal O$ be a characteristic-zero discrete valuation domain, complete for its maximal ideal and with finite residue field $k$, and let $p$ be an odd prime with $p\in\mathfrak m_{\mathcal O}$. Let $\bar\rho$ be a residual representation over $k$ (a rank-two $k$-module with a Galois action factoring through a finite level) that is absolutely irreducible, i.e. irreducible after base change to $\overline k$. Let $S,S_{\min}$ be finite sets of naturals with every element of $S$ prime, $p\in S_{\min}\subseteq S$, such that for primes $q\neq p$ one has $q\in S_{\min}$ exactly when $\bar\rho$ is ramified at $q$, and such that for $q\in S_{\min}$, $q\neq p$, every inertia element at $q$ has characteristic polynomial $(X-1)^2$ in $\bar\rho$. Let $N,L\ge 1$ satisfy: all prime factors of $N$ lie in $S$; $p^2\nmid N$; every $q\in S_{\min}$ with $q\ne p$ divides $N$; every prime $q\ne p$ with $q\notin S_{\min}$ dividing $N$ has $q^2\mid N$; no prime $q\ne p$ has $q^3\mid N$; and $L\mid N$ with $N,L$ having the same prime factors, $q^2\mid N\Rightarrow q^2\mid L$, and $q^3\nmid L$ for all primes $q$. Assume the weight-two cusp forms for $\Gamma_0(N)$ are spanned over $\mathbb C$ by their integral lattice. Let $\theta$ be a ring homomorphism to $k$ from the anemic Hecke algebra [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 S`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18), the $\mathbb Z$-subalgebra of $\operatorname{End}_{\mathbb C}S_2(\Gamma_0(N))$ generated by the Hecke generators away from $S$, such that for every prime $\ell\nmid N$ with $\ell\notin S$, every valuation subring $P$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ over $\ell$ and every $\sigma$ acting as the $\ell$-power map on the residue field of $P$, the characteristic polynomial of $\bar\rho(\sigma)$ is $X^2-\theta(T_\ell)X+\ell$. Let $T=$ [`CuspForm.heckeLocal N S 𝒪 θ`](def/CuspForm_HeckeLocal.html#L131) be the localisation of the anemic Hecke algebra at the multiplicative set attached to $\theta$, let $\pi_T\colon T\to\mathcal O$ be an $\mathcal O$-algebra homomorphism, let $M$ be a $T$-module that is also an $\mathcal O$-module with compatible scalars, and let $B\colon M\times M\to\mathcal O$ be $\mathcal O$-bilinear. Assume [`CuspForm.heckeLocal.IsCornerRealization`](def/CuspForm_HeckeModuleCornerRealization.html#L19) holds for $p,\bar\rho,N,L,S,\theta,M,B$: there are a system $\bar\theta$ of residual eigenvalues for the generators $T_\ell$, $U_q$, $\langle d\rangle$ at level $L$ whose operators on $H^1(\Gamma_H(L),\mathcal O)$ commute, an idempotent splitting of the $\mathcal O$-subalgebra of $\operatorname{End}_{\mathcal O}H^1(\Gamma_H(L),\mathcal O)$ generated by them, an index $i_0$ together with an $\mathcal O$-algebra character of the corresponding corner ring inducing $\bar\theta$, the corner submodule cut out by the idempotent $e_{i_0}$ consisting of parabolic homomorphisms, and an $\mathcal O$-linear isomorphism $e$ of $M$ with that corner submodule; moreover $\bar\theta(T_\ell)=\theta(T_\ell)$ for primes $\ell\notin S$ with $\ell\nmid L$, $\ell\nmid N$, $\bar\theta(U_q)=0$ whenever $q^2\mid L$, $\bar\theta(U_p)\ne 0$ if $p\mid L$ and $\bar\rho$ is ordinary at $p$, $e$ intertwines the action of the image of $T_\ell$ in $T$ on $M$ with the Hecke operator $T_\ell$ on $H^1$, and $B$ is the transport along $e$ of the pairing [`CuspForm.Bfam₀`](def/CuspForm_CornerPairingFamily.html#L140) on parabolic homomorphisms. The conclusion is fourfold: $B(t\cdot m,m')=B(m,t\cdot m')$ for all $t\in T$ and $m,m'\in M$; the map $m\mapsto B(m,-)$ from $M$ to $\operatorname{Hom}_{\mathcal O}(M,\mathcal O)$ is bijective; the submodule of $M$ annihilated by $\ker\pi_T$ is non-zero; and $\operatorname{rank}_{\mathcal O}M$ equals the product of $\operatorname{rank}_{\mathcal O}$ of that submodule with $\operatorname{rank}_{\mathcal O}T$.
--
--   This is the Hecke-module duality input of the level-raising argument: on a corner of the cohomology of a cube-free level $L$ realising the residual eigensystem $\theta$ attached to $\bar\rho$, the cohomological pairing is a perfect pairing under which the Hecke action is self-adjoint, the $\pi_T$-eigenspace is non-zero, and the $\mathcal O$-rank of the module factors as the product of the eigenspace rank with the rank of the localised anemic Hecke algebra. It is used by the statements producing level-raising Hecke modules and the inductive step passing from one corner realisation to the next.
